---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const site = 'https://ewohub.com';
const slug = 'how-stripscore-works';
---

<Base
  title="How StripScore Works: The Real Signals Behind Stripchat's Ranking"
  description="A breakdown of what actually feeds StripScore — viewer count, retention, chat activity, tips, follows, consistency — how the score decays, and what to do about it."
  lang="en"
  hreflang={[
    { lang: 'en', url: `${site}/${slug}` },
    { lang: 'de', url: `${site}/de/${slug}` },
    { lang: 'es', url: `${site}/es/${slug}` },
    { lang: 'ro', url: `${site}/ro/${slug}` },
    { lang: 'uk', url: `${site}/uk/${slug}` },
    { lang: 'ru', url: `${site}/ru/${slug}` },
  ]}
>
  <section class="art-hero">
    <div class="art-orb art-orb--1"></div>
    <div class="art-orb art-orb--2"></div>
    <div class="art-grid"></div>
    <div class="art-hero__inner container">
      <div class="art-meta">
        <span class="art-tag">Guide</span>
        <span class="art-tag art-tag--green">Stripchat</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="art-title">How <span class="art-grad">StripScore</span> Actually Works</h1>
      <p class="art-lead">
        Not what the term means — how the number itself moves. Here's a practical breakdown of the
        signals that build StripScore, how fast they decay, and where models waste effort chasing
        things that don't actually move it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="art-body container">
    <div class="art-layout">
      <aside class="art-toc">
        <p class="art-toc__title">Contents</p>
        <ol class="art-toc__list">
          <li><a href="#signals">The Signals That Build It</a></li>
          <li><a href="#decay">How Fast It Decays</a></li>
          <li><a href="#new-model">StripScore vs. the New Model Boost</a></li>
          <li><a href="#myths">What Doesn't Move It</a></li>
          <li><a href="#checklist">A Practical Checklist</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ol>
        <a href="#cta" class="art-toc__cta">Get a growth strategy →</a>
      </aside>

      <main class="art-main">

        <section id="signals">
          <h2>The Signals That Actually Build StripScore</h2>
          <p>
            Stripchat doesn't publish an exact formula, but the behavior of the Popular category over
            time makes the inputs fairly clear. None of these work in isolation — StripScore is a
            rolling composite, recalculated continuously while you're live.
          </p>

          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">01</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Concurrent viewer count</h3>
              <p>
                The most visible input, but also the most heavily weighted toward <em>sustained</em>
                numbers rather than peaks. A room that holds 40 viewers for an hour outperforms a room
                that spikes to 150 for two minutes and drops to 10.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">02</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Watch time / retention</h3>
              <p>
                How long each viewer actually stays matters more than how many click in. High
                click-through with fast drop-off (common with bot or low-intent traffic) reads as a
                negative signal, not a neutral one — it tells the algorithm your room doesn't retain
                the audience it was shown to.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">03</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Chat activity</h3>
              <p>
                Messages, reactions, and general chat pace signal an engaged room versus a passively
                watched one. Rooms that prompt conversation — asking questions, responding to
                usernames, running polls — generate more of this signal per viewer than silent streams.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">04</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Tips and goal completions</h3>
              <p>
                Direct monetization events carry real weight, since they're the platform's strongest
                proxy for "this room is delivering value." Frequent smaller tips throughout a stream
                tend to sustain the score better than one large tip followed by a quiet stretch.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">05</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Follows gained while live</h3>
              <p>
                New follows during an active session are treated as a stronger signal than your total
                follower count — the algorithm cares more about "is this room converting viewers right
                now" than a static number from months ago.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="reason-card">
            <div class="reason-num">06</div>
            <div class="reason-content">
              <h3>Streaming consistency</h3>
              <p>
                Rooms that go live on a predictable schedule build a baseline the algorithm trusts,
                which shows up as steadier placement even on average sessions. Irregular streamers see
                more volatile ranking swings session to session, even at similar performance levels.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="decay">
          <h2>How Fast StripScore Decays</h2>
          <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--warning">
            <p>
              StripScore is not a bank balance — it doesn't accumulate and hold. It's closer to a
              rolling average that decays quickly once a stream ends and continues decaying the longer
              you're offline. A huge session three days ago has essentially zero influence on your
              placement today. This is why one exceptional stream doesn't "carry" you — consistency
              beats occasional peaks because the score is always measuring recent, not lifetime,
              performance.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="new-model">
          <h2>StripScore vs. the "New Model" Boost</h2>
          <div class="glass-card">
            <p>
              New accounts get placement in the separate "New Models" category for roughly their first
              14 days, which is a distinct visibility mechanism, not a StripScore multiplier. It's a
              guaranteed placement window, independent of how strong your organic score is yet. Once
              that window closes, you're ranked purely on the signals above, competing in the general
              Popular pool. Models who build strong session habits <em>during</em> the New Model window
              tend to see the smoothest transition, since consistency and retention habits carry over
              even though the guaranteed placement doesn't.
            </p>
            <p style="margin-top:.875rem;">
              See the full day-by-day breakdown in our <a href="/stripchat-first-14-days-guide">first 14 days guide →</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="myths">
          <h2>What Doesn't Move It (Even Though It Feels Like It Should)</h2>
          <div class="two-col-box">
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--bad">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">MYTH</p>
              <p>Stacking more tags gets you seen by more categories, which raises your score.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--good">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">REALITY</p>
              <p>Tags affect discoverability, not the score itself. Irrelevant tags can actually hurt retention when the wrong viewers click in and leave fast.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="two-col-box">
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--bad">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">MYTH</p>
              <p>Buying viewers or using a "traffic boost" bot raises StripScore.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--good">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">REALITY</p>
              <p>Bot traffic produces near-zero watch time and no chat/tip activity, which drags the retention signal down. See our <a href="/stripchat-promo">full review of these services →</a></p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="two-col-box">
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--bad">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">MYTH</p>
              <p>Streaming longer hours always means a higher score.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--good">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">REALITY</p>
              <p>Long low-engagement stretches drag the average down. A focused 2-hour session with real interaction outperforms 6 quiet hours.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="checklist">
          <h2>A Practical Checklist</h2>
          <div class="checklist">
            <p class="checklist__title">Session habits that actually move StripScore</p>
            <ul>
              <li class="ok"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Stream at the same times most days — predictability builds baseline trust</li>
              <li class="ok"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Open with direct engagement (greet by name, ask a question) in the first minutes</li>
              <li class="ok"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Run small, frequent goals instead of one distant big goal</li>
              <li class="ok"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Prioritize retaining current viewers over chasing new clicks</li>
              <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg> Don't pad session length past the point of real engagement</li>
              <li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg> Don't use bought traffic or bot viewers to fake a spike</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="cta">
          <div class="art-cta">
            <div class="art-cta__orb"></div>
            <div class="art-cta__inner">
              <span class="art-cta__badge">Want This Managed For You</span>
              <h2>We build the session habits that move your ranking</h2>
              <p>Scheduling, engagement pacing, goal structure — the same signals covered here, run consistently instead of guessed at.</p>
              <div class="art-cta__actions">
                <a href="/model-promotion" class="art-cta__btn--primary btn btn-primary">See model promotion →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="faq" class="faq-section">
          <h2>FAQ</h2>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>Does StripScore reset to zero when I go offline?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>Not to a hard zero, but it decays heavily the longer you're offline, so a long gap functions close to a reset in practice.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>Is StripScore the same thing as the New Model boost?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>No — the New Model window is a separate, time-limited placement guarantee. StripScore is the ongoing organic score that takes over once that window ends.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-chevron" aria-expanded="false">
              <span>Can one great stream undo a week of low viewership?</span>
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M5 7.5l5 5 5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-body"><p>It helps that session's placement, but because the score decays quickly, it won't carry forward much past a day or two. Consistency matters more than any single peak.</p></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Related Articles</h2>
          <div class="related-grid">
            <a href="/stripscore-cam-rank-explained" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">❓</span>
              <span>What Is Stripscore? Terminology Explained</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/how-cam-algorithm-ranks-rooms" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">📊</span>
              <span>How Cam Algorithms Rank Rooms (All Platforms)</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/stripchat-first-14-days-guide" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">🗓</span>
              <span>Your First 14 Days on Stripchat</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/raise-your-room-ranking-score" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">📈</span>
              <span>How to Raise Your Room's Ranking Score</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/stripchat-popular-new-model-visibility" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">👀</span>
              <span>Why New Models Show Up in Popular</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/why-low-viewers-webcam" class="related-card">
              <span class="related-card__icon">📉</span>
              <span>Why Your Webcam Room Has Low Viewers</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
